WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,564
Welcome to the Kony three-six-five Last Man Standing Gameweek One review.

2
00:00:04,514 --> 00:00:09,402
The opening weekend is complete, and four players have already been sent six feet deep.

3
00:00:09,402 --> 00:00:16,579
The popular choice was Arsenal, who delivered comfortably with a three-nil win over Coventry City, sending eleven players safely through.

4
00:00:16,579 --> 00:00:27,326
Hub really showed the casuals what a Round One testicular fortitude looks like, picking Ipswich Town, who beat Sunderland two-one, sending Tom Mahon out before he's even had the chance to rekindle his uni friendships.

5
00:00:27,326 --> 00:00:30,161
More solo picks from people who know ball.

6
00:00:30,161 --> 00:00:41,199
Chris Gill got the Seagulls flying, Jordan Padel relied on fellow ginger David Moyes to book his place in the next round, and Alf just ended up on the better side of a bloke-versus-geezer West London derby on Monday night.

7
00:00:41,199 --> 00:00:46,679
Manchester United got mauled by the Tigers, sending Leicester and newly engaged Tom Davies out.

8
00:00:46,679 --> 00:00:49,882
He might be going home, but it's not an empty house.

9
00:00:49,882 --> 00:00:56,579
Speaking of empty, Cam came in, emptied a full clip of hate on Alf, and has now left the building after Forest failed him.

10
00:00:56,579 --> 00:01:05,462
So, after Gameweek One: four down, fifteen remain, and it's time to either pick or let the wheel decide, as we're heading into Gameweek Two, baby!

11
00:01:05,462 --> 00:01:09,480
The next deadline is Friday the twenty-eighth of August at seven p.m.

12
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:13,922
British Summer Time, one hour before Crystal Palace versus Manchester City.

13
00:01:13,922 --> 00:01:18,130
This has been your Kony three-six-five Last Man Standing round review.
